\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Frozen auxiliary V117 country cases, separate from the primary sixteen cities. Top: retained score intervals. Bottom: all twenty utility differences, first city minus second; seven exclude zero. Positive differences favour the first city; negative differences favour the second. Grey ranges leave direction unresolved. School resource retains 2024--25 school-location all-age XI--XII counts and nominal teacher-headcount allocation, not FTE. Living cost and housing use 2025 Numbeo aggregates; air uses 2021 WHO monitoring means; broadband uses the September 2026 index (July--September test window). Source years, boundaries and populations differ. Ranges are conditional identification bounds, not confidence intervals; neither pair identifies a necessary overall winner \cite  {legacycase,numbeocase,whocase}.}}{17}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:country-contrasts}{{3}{17}{Frozen auxiliary V117 country cases, separate from the primary sixteen cities. Top: retained score intervals. Bottom: all twenty utility differences, first city minus second; seven exclude zero. Positive differences favour the first city; negative differences favour the second. Grey ranges leave direction unresolved. School resource retains 2024--25 school-location all-age XI--XII counts and nominal teacher-headcount allocation, not FTE. Living cost and housing use 2025 Numbeo aggregates; air uses 2021 WHO monitoring means; broadband uses the September 2026 index (July--September test window). Source years, boundaries and populations differ. Ranges are conditional identification bounds, not confidence intervals; neither pair identifies a necessary overall winner \cite {legacycase,numbeocase,whocase}}{figure.3}{}}
